    Map a score to an achievement badge.

    1000 or more gives 'gold', 500 or more 'silver', 100 or more 'bronze',
    anything lower 'none'. Plain ints and numeric strings like '750' or ' 250 '
    work normally, while None, empty or whitespace-only strings, non-numeric
    text such as 'abc' or '12.5', and wrong types like lists or dicts all
    return default instead of raising.
